obituaries.full_text:
He is survived by seven sons: George of Kokomo, John of Indianapolis, Delmer 
  of Greentown, Cloyd of Greentown, William of South Bend and Leslie of Brazil; 
  two daughters, Mrs. Edith Bogue of Kokomo and Mrs. Minnie Perkins of Greentown; 
  two brothers, Will of Kokomo and Ellsworth of Tipton, and one sister, Mrs. Lou 
  Hunsinger of Elwood.

Mr. Greenage is survived by his wife of 29 years, Anna M. (Humphries) Greenage, 
  his daughter, Michelle Greenage, and his son, John Greenage Jr., all of Smyrna; 
  his brothers and sisters-in-law; and an abundance of nieces and nephews.
